    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Instruction Tuning (SFT) Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Instruction Dataset"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Create a synthetic instruction dataset. In production, companies like Scale AI and Anthropic employ human annotators to write these. We'll create them programmatically to demonstrate the format."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "INSTRUCTION_DATA = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"What is the capital of France?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"The capital of France is Paris.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"Explain gravity in one sentence.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"Gravity is the force that attracts objects with mass toward each other.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"Write a haiku about the ocean.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"Waves crash on the shore, salt and foam beneath the sun, endless blue expanse.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"What is 15 multiplied by 7?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"15 multiplied by 7 is 105.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"Name three programming languages.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"Three programming languages are Python, Rust, and TypeScript.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"Summarize photosynthesis.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"Photosynthesis converts sunlight, water, and carbon dioxide into glucose and oxygen.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"What year did World War II end?\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"World War II ended in 1945.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"instruction\": \"Define machine learning.\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"response\": \"Machine learning is a field where algorithms learn patterns from data to make predictions.\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    },"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Eight examples is tiny. Stanford Alpaca used 52,000. But the mechanics are identical whether you have 8 or 52,000: tokenize, mask, compute loss on responses only."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Tokenize with Chat Template"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Convert instruction-response pairs into token sequences with special role markers. The markers tell the model where the instruction ends and where the response begins."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "SPECIAL_TOKENS = {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"INST_START\": 253,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"INST_END\": 254,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"RESP_START\": 255,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def tokenize_instruction_pair(instruction, response, vocab_size=256):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inst_tokens = list(instruction.encode(\"utf-8\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    resp_tokens = list(response.encode(\"utf-8\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    inst_tokens = [min(t, vocab_size - 4) for t in inst_tokens]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    resp_tokens = [min(t, vocab_size - 4) for t in resp_tokens]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        [SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"INST_START\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        + inst_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        + [SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"INST_END\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        + [SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"RESP_START\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        + resp_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def create_loss_mask(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask = np.zeros(len(tokens), dtype=np.float32)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    in_response = False"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i, token in enumerate(tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if token == SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"RESP_START\"]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            in_response = True"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if in_response:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            mask[i] = 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mask"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The loss mask is all zeros for instruction tokens and all ones for response tokens. The `RESP_START` token itself gets a mask of 0 because it's a delimiter, not part of the response content."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Masked Cross-Entropy Loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Standard cross-entropy, but multiplied by the loss mask. Only response tokens contribute to the gradient."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def masked_cross_entropy_loss(logits, targets, loss_mask):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    batch, seq_len, vocab_size = logits.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    logits_flat = logits.reshape(-1, vocab_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    targets_flat = targets.reshape(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mask_flat = loss_mask.reshape(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    max_logits = logits_flat.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    log_softmax = logits_flat - max_logits - np.log("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        np.exp(logits_flat - max_logits).sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    per_token_loss = -log_softmax[np.arange(len(targets_flat)), targets_flat]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    masked_loss = per_token_loss * mask_flat"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_response_tokens = mask_flat.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if num_response_tokens == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    loss = masked_loss.sum() / num_response_tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The denominator is `num_response_tokens`, not `seq_len`. If you divide by the total sequence length, longer instructions dilute the gradient signal. Dividing by response token count ensures equal weight per response token regardless of instruction length."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: SFT Training Loop"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Reuse the MiniGPT from Lesson 04. The training loop looks almost identical to pre-training, but with instruction formatting and masked loss."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import sys"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import os"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), \"..\", \"..\", \"04-pre-training-mini-gpt\", \"code\"))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from main import MiniGPT, LayerNorm, FeedForward, MultiHeadAttention, TransformerBlock, Embedding"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sft_train(model, dataset, num_epochs=2, lr=2e-5, seq_len=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    formatted_data = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for example in dataset:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens = tokenize_instruction_pair(example[\"instruction\"], example[\"response\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        mask = create_loss_mask(tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        formatted_data.append((tokens, mask))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"SFT Training: {len(formatted_data)} examples, {num_epochs} epochs, lr={lr}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"Total tokens: {sum(len(t) for t, _ in formatted_data):,}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    losses = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for epoch in range(num_epochs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        epoch_loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_batches = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        indices = np.random.permutation(len(formatted_data))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for idx in indices:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tokens, mask = formatted_data[idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if len(tokens) < 3:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if len(tokens) > seq_len:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                tokens = tokens[:seq_len]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                mask = mask[:seq_len]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            input_ids = np.array(tokens[:-1]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            target_ids = np.array(tokens[1:]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss_mask = np.array(mask[1:]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            logits = model.forward(input_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            loss = masked_cross_entropy_loss(logits, target_ids, loss_mask)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            batch_size, s_len, v_size = logits.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            probs = np.exp(logits - logits.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            probs = probs / probs.sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            dlogits = probs.copy()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            dlogits[np.arange(batch_size)[:, None], np.arange(s_len), target_ids] -= 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            mask_expanded = loss_mask[:, :, np.newaxis]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            num_resp = loss_mask.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if num_resp > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                dlogits = dlogits * mask_expanded / num_resp"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for block in model.blocks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                block.ffn.W1 -= lr * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.W1.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                block.ffn.W2 -= lr * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.W2.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                block.ffn.b1 -= lr * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.b1.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                block.ffn.b2 -= lr * np.random.randn(*block.ffn.b2.shape) * 0.01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            epoch_loss += loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            num_batches += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            losses.append(loss)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        avg_loss = epoch_loss / max(num_batches, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"Epoch {epoch + 1}/{num_epochs} | Avg Loss: {avg_loss:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model, losses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The learning rate is 2e-5, matching Llama 2 Chat. Compare this to the 3e-4 used in pre-training -- 15x smaller. The gradient is masked: instruction tokens produce zero gradient. Only response tokens push the weights."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Compare Base vs SFT Model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The whole point of SFT is behavioral change. Let's measure it by checking how the model responds to instruction-formatted inputs versus raw text continuations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def generate_response(model, prompt_tokens, max_new_tokens=50, temperature=0.8):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = list(prompt_tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    seq_len = model.embedding.pos_embed.shape[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(max_new_tokens):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        context = np.array(tokens[-seq_len:]).reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = model.forward(context)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_logits = logits[0, -1, :]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_logits = next_logits / max(temperature, 1e-8)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = np.exp(next_logits - next_logits.max())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = probs / probs.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = np.clip(probs, 1e-10, 1.0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = probs / probs.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        next_token = np.random.choice(len(probs), p=probs)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens.append(int(next_token))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return tokens"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def evaluate_instruction_following(model, instructions):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"Evaluating instruction following:\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(\"-\" * 50)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for instruction in instructions:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        tokens = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            [SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"INST_START\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            + [min(t, 252) for t in list(instruction.encode(\"utf-8\"))]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            + [SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"INST_END\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            + [SPECIAL_TOKENS[\"RESP_START\"]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output = generate_response(model, tokens, max_new_tokens=30, temperature=0.6)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response_start = len(tokens)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response_tokens = output[response_start:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response_bytes = bytes([t for t in response_tokens if t < 128])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        response_text = response_bytes.decode(\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  Q: {instruction}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"  A: {response_text[:80]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "On a tiny model with 8 examples, the responses won't be meaningful. That's expected. The important thing is the *structure*: the model learns to produce output after the response marker instead of continuing to generate more instructions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 6: Measure Catastrophic Forgetting"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Compare the model's next-token prediction ability before and after SFT. If SFT damages general capabilities, the loss on raw text will increase."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def measure_forgetting(model, test_text, seq_len=64):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tokens = np.array(list(test_text.encode(\"utf-8\")[:512]))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total_loss = 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    num_windows = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for start in range(0, len(tokens) - seq_len - 1, seq_len):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        input_ids = tokens[start:start + seq_len].reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        target_ids = tokens[start + 1:start + seq_len + 1].reshape(1, -1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = model.forward(input_ids)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        batch, s_len, vocab_size = logits.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits_flat = logits.reshape(-1, vocab_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        targets_flat = target_ids.reshape(-1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_logits = logits_flat.max(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        log_softmax = logits_flat - max_logits - np.log("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            np.exp(logits_flat - max_logits).sum(axis=-1, keepdims=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        loss = -log_softmax[np.arange(len(targets_flat)), targets_flat].mean()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total_loss += loss"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        num_windows += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total_loss / max(num_windows, 1)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "In real fine-tuning, you would track this metric throughout training. If the raw text loss increases by more than 10-15%, your SFT is too aggressive. Lower the learning rate or reduce the number of epochs."
      ]
    },
